/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 103 0 R
/E (I addressed the need to demonstrate how a DC load can be disconnected when a monitored input exceeds a set limit. I designed and simulated the circuit in Tinkercad, programmed the Arduino Uno, and connected the motor, TIP120 transistor, LCD, LEDs, buzzer, and potentiometer. This project helped me practise Arduino programming, circuit wiring, analog input reading, PWM control, and LCD interfacing. The simulation runs the motor below the set threshold and stops it above the threshold, while displaying and signaling the system status. The potentiometer represents the load signal; it does not measure actual motor current.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [0]
>>
